Greetings, friends!

Today we're updating ATOM RPG with a fair quantity of new fixes and optimizations, as well as the highly awaited, fully reworked Polish localization many of you were expecting for a long time now. 

Please, enjoy! And should there be any feedback about the new translation, please feel free to message us at support@atomrpg.com or use the Steam forums. 

Best wishes, Atom Team

Change log:

- Added reworked Polish language localization;
- Fixed various minor typos and errors in the game texts;
- Optimized game to perform better on low-end hardware;
- Fixed several minor community-reported bugs.
- The game resources were repacked to speed up loading time on older HDD.

Change log: 

- Added Ukrainian localization;
- Fixed errors in Italian localization;
- Fixed issue with items disappearing from inventory after using the guide's map;
- Fixed critical issue when entering Death Tunnel;
- Item duplication bug fixed;
- Fixed battle grid disappearing rare bug;
- Radiation debuff now goes away correctly after healing rad. poisoning;
- Music in sex scenes now works properly;
- Visual glitches removed on random encounter maps;
- Visuals of Shadow attacks fixed;
- General visual glitches resolved;
- Gamepad issues reported by players fixed;
- Various minor bugs fixed.

[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/28203835/6e405b8cb2fc683ef5b0a07d4d5ad2aa79efd0cc.jpg[/img]

Greetings, friends!

The moment has come and our second game, which directly continues the series, [b]ATOM RPG: Trudograd[/b] has finally been released from Early Access.

Planned as a small DLC, Trudograd quickly grew thanks to your suggestions, and currently boasts the following traits:
[list]
[*] [b]Ability to continue playing as your ATOM RPG character[/b] - for this you must make a save file after beating ATOM RPG’s last boss and upload it into Trudograd via a helpful menu;
[*] A vast open world, containing 45+ populated locations, from a snowy post apocalyptic megapolis and its outskirts to secret Soviet military bunkers, a large pirate tanker in the frozen sea and a mysterious island, among many more;
[*] 30+ combat-only locations where players will get to fight tens of foe varieties from mercenaries to merciless mutants;
[*] 300+ characters, each with a unique portrait and branching dialogue;
[*] 200+ quests, most with multiple solutions and outcomes;
[*] Fully voiced visual text quests with branching plots and unique hand made artwork;
[*] 100+ models of distinct weaponry with 75+ weapon mods for further customization;
[*] 3 unique powered Soviet-style exoskeleton armor suits, with 20+ ways to customize and modify them for any playstyle;
[*] 45+ hours of gameplay with heightened replayability compared to our studio’s first game;
[*] Original soundtrack;
[/list]
...And many more additions that make Trudograd a great single player RPG experience!

Now we want to tell you about all the new packs, kits and bundles you might see on our game’s page.


[url=https://store.steampowered.com/bundle/22413/ATOM_RPG_2in1_Edition/][img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/28203835/598dca3ba7493cfc66b1e6efbffad013f1a88502.png[/img][/url]
This did not happen often, however we did get messages from people saying they want to wait until the release of Trudograd to check out ATOM RPG. Probably in order to play both titles one straight after another. For those folks, we have created the special [b]ATOM RPG 2-in-1 Edition[/b] which features both of our studio’s games. It being a bundle makes it easier to purchase, and allowed us to add a special little discount to boot!


[url=https://store.steampowered.com/app/1713870/ATOM_RPG_Trudograd__Supporter_Pack/][img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/28203835/6260855972068cc32df536d58046a19e49fad6c2.png[/img][/url]
Also, just like with ATOM RPG, we have decided to make an optional purely cosmetic DLC for Trudograd, called the [b]Supporter Pack[/b]. This kit was made solely for people who wish to support our studio further even after buying our game. The items in it are purely cosmetic and do not affect the player’s experience. They are only there as a small gift of gratitude for additional support, which is always greatly appreciated. Thank you so much!


[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/28203835/0b1508ff56ea5e8fe9e5e311c0e1a0f8e4283003.png[/img]
Finally, as you know, those of you who supported us in Early Access, received a free cosmetic DLC called [b]Veteran’s Pack[/b]. 


[url=https://store.steampowered.com/app/1741760/ATOM_RPG_Trudograd__War_Supply_Pack/][img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/28203835/044a28a7c9ce4885ab6b326ac8526bf25b8bd0b5.png[/img][/url]
For those of you who missed this opportunity but still want to have something similar to it, or simply wish to support us, we have made the [b]War Supply Pack[/b], which features similar items with similar functions. 

Just as before, nothing in the War Supply Pack will change, add to or improve your gaming experience with Trudograd. It is simply a cosmetic addition made in thanks for purely optional, additional support. 

We really hope you enjoy our game!

[b]Welcome to Trudograd![/b] And let there be… ATOM!

Hello friends!
It's time for another minor update of the game, which may prove very significant for those of you who patiently waited for the unofficial German language translation of the game. 
Thanks to our amazing fan translation team which can be found here: [url=https://steamcommunity.com/app/552620/discussions/1/1780513643845875564/][CLICK][/url] we can finally release the first version of the translation publicly. We hope it is to your liking, but if you find any issues please share your feedback here: [url=https://steamcommunity.com/app/552620/discussions/1/2999920878441481630][CLICK] [/url]

Other changes this update brings are: 

- Loading times optimization;
- Memory usage optimization;
- Small controller problems fixed;

Thank you for being with us and let there be ATOM!

Greetings, friends!

While work on [url=https://store.steampowered.com/app/1139940/ATOM_RPG_Trudograd/]ATOM RPG: Trudograd[/url] is our main priority at the moment, we did notice a few rare bugs and glitches in our original game thanks to you guys contacting us with reports, and therefore we're publishing this little fix, which is sure to smooth things out, increase FPS and make [b]ATOM RPG[/b] much more pleasant for all those who had performance issues in the past. This update also fixes a bunch of very rare, hard to hit bugs you helped us find. The full changelog is presented below. 

- Now your companions don't leave the fight if they have an order;
- Fixes to localization;
- Now there is a hint for controllers in the option menu;
- Fixed a lot of bugs when playing with the controller;
- The game loads faster;
- Fixed a big bug with getting achievements;
- Fixed the pop-up text shimmering when moving the camera;
- A lot of locations are optimized for better fps;
- Fixed the grass textures that caused a graphic glitch when moving the camera (thank you to our community for finding it);
- A new material is added for the moat in Otradnoye;
- Fixed the health bar position for the smaller creatures.

[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/28203835/03b5ef89771080f0b1723cafc35a19835ff354d7.png[/img]
[url={STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/28203835/31a96a27871ee77345dbc1a0b89c24c723795f79.jpg][img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/28203835/de24074042f898a44d2033a7c61f1fb880198a02.jpg[/img][/url]

Thank you for being the most helpful community there is. And let there be ATOM!

[b]Changelog:[/b]
[list]
[*] Fixed loading localization mods;
[*] Fixed twitching of characters at low frame rates;
[*] Optimized the land rendering queue;
[*] Reduced processor load;
[*] Updated version of Unity to fix launch problems on some PCs;
[*] Fixed a problem with unnecessary recalculation of the position of the text while the camera is moving;
[*] Changes in Polish localization;
[*] Fixed impassable places in different locations;
[*] Fixed places where items fell under the map;
[*] Fixed revolver models;
[*] Updated some old portraits;
[*] Fixed synchronization bugs with cloud saving;
[*] Fixed some graphical bugs with the intersection of decals and objects;
[*] Fixed position of interface objects in TV mode;
[*] Fixed selection of body parts when aiming a shot via console controlsl;
[*] Fixed animation of picking up an item when quick clicking.
[/list]

Greetings, friends!

As many of you already know, we love bringing temporary optional events into our game on special occasions, both to spice up the game you already know through and through as well as to have an excuse to give you some brand new “toys” to play with :)

This time the special event we wish to commemorate with a free update is the end of this pretty arduous Winter.

The new content that will be made available for it is going to be a rather large map in the Dead City, where you will get to do a lot of exploring, fighting and surviving for a chance to acquire several new weapons, meet new friends and enemies, as well as uncover a pre-war military installation.

To get to the event map you will have to travel to Dead City and find a new marker between the store and the playground.

[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/28203835/22f121fdb8ae159b7b13088400dcc10e4c4cf521.png[/img]
As always, if temporary events aren’t your thing, this one can be turned off in the menu. It will disappear from the game in 30 days on its own as well.

This update also brings some minor fixes to the game, as well as new optimization for low-end PCs.

We would also like to use this occasion to remind our German-speaking players that the community translation for the game, led by a group of our fans is almost finished. You can check on their amazing progress and wish them the best of luck in the forum!

Have a great Spring, friends. And as always, let there be ATOM!

